# Cloudflare R2 credentials — TEMPLATE. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored twice over (`*.local` and an explicit entry). This
# example file carries NO values and is safe to commit.
#
# A key that reaches a public repo is compromised even after you delete the line —
# git keeps history and forks keep copies. If it ever happens: ROTATE the key.
# Do not just remove it.

# From the Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Overview. A 32-char hex string.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=

# The bucket name you created. Suggested: chandparaaa-media
R2_BUCKET=

# https://<R2_ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# Note: the S3 API endpoint, NOT the public r2.dev URL.
R2_ENDPOINT=

# R2 → Manage API Tokens → Create API Token.
# Scope it to **Object Read & Write** on **this one bucket** — not account-wide.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not a secret, and NOT set here — this one belongs in the build environment,
# because Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed vars to client code.
#
#   VITE_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://media.chandparaaa.in
#
# Leave it UNSET for local development: src/lib/mediaManifest.js then falls back
# to the site's own BASE_URL and serves from public/projects/, so the site works
# offline with no bucket at all. Set it only for production builds, once the
# bucket is populated and verified.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Token hygiene, from the pack's hard-won notes:
#
#   - TWO tokens, not one shared: a laptop token here, and a separate automation
#     token in GitHub Actions secrets. When one leaks you rotate one, and you know
#     immediately which surface leaked it.
#   - Rotate roughly every six months. Create and VERIFY the new token BEFORE
#     retiring the old one, or you take your own pipeline down at the worst moment.
#   - NEVER pass --prune from CI. A runner holds only what it just encoded, so a
#     prune there would delete the rest of the project's media from the bucket.
